LAST-MODIFIED:20260306T162440Z
UID:10001514-1781341200-1781355600@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Wild on the Water (Huntersville)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF’s Charlotte Wildlife Stewards chapter for its annual fundraiser\, Wild on the Water! Paddle along with like-minded nature lovers\, learn from experienced naturalists\, and raise funds for local wildlife projects. \nFollowing the fun on the water\, enjoy a delicious lunch followed by a raffle of great prizes. Each paddler will receive one raffle ticket with their $75 registration. Receive additional raffle tickets for every $25 donated. Purchase additional raffle tickets on the day of the event for $30 each. Raffle prizes are valued between $50 and $100. \nEarly Bird Registration: Register by April 1 to be entered into a drawing to win a Smart Bird Feeder! This feeder comes with a solar-powered camera capable of still photos and videos plus added AI recognition! \nRegistration and entry fees are not required for children who will join you on the water\, but please use the paddling partner section on the next page to let us know how many children will accompany you so we have an accurate headcount for lunch. \nA limited number of kayaks and canoes are available on a first come\, first served basis. If a second paddler will join you in a canoe they must register separately. Registered participants may bring their own kayak\, canoe\, or paddle board if desired. You will have an opportunity to indicate your vessel of choice below. \n* Personal floatation devices (PFDs) are required for all paddlers and passengers.* If reserving one of our boats\, a PFD will be provided. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/wild-on-the-water-huntersville/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/WOW-CWS_2022_logo-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
